      "title": "Determining Whether Three Vectors are Coplanar"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "fa65479b-814f-5df8-b085-4ce2861f4fb2",
      ":question/problem": "Find $k$ given that the vectors $a=\u27e80,0,-1\u27e9$, $b=\u27e8-1,-2,3\u27e9$, and $c=\u27e82,k,1\u27e9$ are coplanar.\n\n$k=${{field-1}}",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "98600296-9675-5896-9a26-450bc4d86d37",
          ":answer-field/key": "field-1",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/blank",
          ":answer-field/choices": [
            {
              ":answer/id": "164064c7-211f-5af5-a157-9ede3b70c2e6",
              ":answer/type": ":answer.type/math",
              ":answer/value": "4"
            }
          ],
          ":answer-field/correct": [
            ":answer/id",
            "164064c7-211f-5af5-a157-9ede3b70c2e6"
          ]
        }
      ],
      ":question/worked-solution": "Computing the triple product, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}a\\cdot(b\\times c)&=|\\begin{aligned}0 & 0 & -1 \\\\ -1 & -2 & 3 \\\\ 2 & k & 1\\end{aligned}|\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-2 & 3 \\\\ k & 1\\end{aligned}|)+((0)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & 3 \\\\ 2 & 1\\end{aligned}|)+((-1)\\cdot |\\begin{aligned}-1 & -2 \\\\ 2 & k\\end{aligned}|)\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot ((-2)\\cdot (1)-(3)\\cdot (k)))+((0)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (1)-(3)\\cdot (2)))+((-1)\\cdot ((-1)\\cdot (k)-(-2)\\cdot (2)))\\\\ &=((0)\\cdot (-3k-2))+((0)\\cdot (-7))+((-1)\\cdot (4-k))\\\\ &=(0)+(0)+(k-4)\\\\ &=k-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThree vectors are coplanar if and only if their triple product is zero:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}k-4&=0\\\\ k&=4\\\\ k&=4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the three vectors are coplanar if and only if $k=4.$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy"
    },
